1
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:09,000
[opening theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:14,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

3
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:43,000
[singer singing in English]

4
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:41,000
[narrator]
With the death of King Meruem,

5
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:46,000
the battle between Chimera Ants
and humans was finally over.

6
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:49,000
The Republic of East Gorteau and the NGL

7
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:53,000
were placed under the provisional rule
of the International Security Agency,

8
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:56,000
effectively dismantling both countries.

9
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:05,000
The Mitene Union's
three remaining countries

10
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:08,000
divided East Gorteau's assets equally,

11
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:14,000
and after brief negotiations, agreed
to have joint control over the territory.

12
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:16,000
As for the NGL,

13
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:20,000
there was a proposal to permanently
designate all uninhabited land

14
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:24,000
as a nature reserve, in hopes
that this would prevent future conflict,

15
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:28,000
and it was quickly approved
in the international assembly.

16
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:33,000
It was also agreed that the nature reserve
would be placed under the jurisdiction

17
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:36,000
of the Hunter Association.

18
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:48,000
[Welfin] You sure about this?

19
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:51,000
[Bloster] You bet!

20
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:53,000
I'm gonna live right here, no question!

21
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:02,000
I don't remember Gyro, but still,
this place just feels like home.

22
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:13,000
and didn't work for Gyro.

23
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:18,000
[Welfin] Well, I'm not gonna
twist your arm.

24
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:22,000
This is probably safer
than the other countries.

25
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:25,000
No doubt about that.

26
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:30,000
Just one good look at me, and the
peacekeepers would arrest me on the spot.

27
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:52,000
Hmm? What are you talking about?

28
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Hey! Are you done? Let's get moving.

29
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:56,000
She's such a brat.

30
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:58,000
Just give me a minute!

31
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:09,000
those like you and Hina, who do remember,
you all seem a little,

32
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:11,000
I don't know… different.

33
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:16,000
Maybe it's the light in your eyes,
how you look off into the distance.

34
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:21,000
I can tell just by looking at you, like,

35
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:24,000
"Yeah, this guy remembers his past."

36
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:43,000
It's that she's not able to.

37
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:49,000
She's probably a little kid.

38
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:03,000
We might not see each other again.
So, take care, okay?

39
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:08,000
I will.

40
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:12,000
Just don't die… until you're dead.

41
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:22,000
That's always been my favorite phrase.

42
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,000
[Welfin] Oh! Right!

43
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:34,000
[Bloster] So it's like
"seize the day," huh?

44
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:38,000
-[Welfin] Huh. Later!
-[Bloster] Yeah!

45
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:01,000
[wind blowing]

46
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:07,000
[Hina humming]

47
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:26,000
-Wait, do I know them? Guess not.
-Huh?

48
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:30,000
[chuckles] No point in thinking
about the dead, right?

49
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:33,000
Keep looking forward! Full speed ahead!

50
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:42,000
Are you positive we can make it safely
to the harbor?

51
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:48,000
Yes. It's a government vehicle, so
I'll show my card and they'll let us pass.

52
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:53,000
[sighs] Before long,
I'll be living in Meteor City.

53
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:02,000
[gulps]

54
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:04,000
[sighs]

55
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:07,000
Just a little bit longer to go.

56
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:24,000
And you know what that means,

57
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:28,000
that we're gonna be back on top
in no time at all!

58
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:29,000
Yay!

59
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:32,000
[Hina chuckles]

60
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:37,000
Well, I envy your unbridled optimism.
I just wish that I shared it.

61
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:40,000
"Optimism"? Got that right!

62
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:55,000
-[Hina giggles]
-[tires screech]

63
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:57,000
[Bizeff] Knock it off!

64
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:09,000
Might as well enjoy… whatever is next.

65
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:11,000
[Welfin] Yeah, that's the spirit!

66
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:25,000
in the hopes of finding Gyro.

67
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:19,000
[gasps]

68
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:40,000
[doors slam]

69
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:44,000
[Bloster sighs] Well, I can't blame 'em.

70
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:55,000
Hey! People of the NGL,

71
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:05,000
I promise, we mean you no harm!

72
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:09,000
I've got something I need to ask you!

73
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:22,000
All right!
Sounds like you speak our language.

74
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:24,000
Tell us who you are.

75
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:27,000
Uh, well…

76
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:40,000
You're the only ones I can turn to.

77
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:46,000
[mellow music playing]

78
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:58,000
[imperceptible]

79
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:08,000
[gasps]

80
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:16,000
[sobbing]

81
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:57,000
[sobbing]

82
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:00,000
Reina?

83
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:03,000
How did…

84
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:07,000
How did you know?

85
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:26,000
Reina! Reina!

86
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:27,000
[thud]

87
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:29,000
[sobbing]

88
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:31,000
[Shidore] How could you tell it was me?

89
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:33,000
[mother] I'm your mother, Reina!

90
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:36,000
Of course, I could tell! How could I not?

91
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:39,000
[both sobbing]

92
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:55,000
He told the monster to go away,
and he told me to run.

93
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:59,000
He kept me safe!
If it hadn't been for him…

94
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:18,000
I'm the one who's sorry.

95
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:21,000
Sorry I wasn't there with you,

96
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:24,000
sorry I couldn't keep you safe.

97
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:29,000
Reina dear, welcome back home!

98
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:36,000
Why don't we all go eat together?

99
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:47,000
-[woman] Hello!
-[gasps]

100
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:49,000
Would you like to stay and join us?

101
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:02,000
We want to thank you for what you've done.

102
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:06,000
[Bloster] Look, I'm not that kinda guy,
okay? See ya!

103
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:18,000
Damn it! Now we're even. It's over.

104
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:27,000
Damn that stupid octopus!
He never should've let me live!

105
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:36,000
[dramatic music playing]

106
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:53,000
[Shidore] Thank you!

107
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:57,000
Come on.

108
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:18,000
What is this? Why am I crying?

109
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:26,000
[narrator] Reina and Bloster,
home at last.

110
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:41,000
Look like the politicians have somehow
turned this into an international crisis.

111
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:58,000
[Colt] Is that right?

112
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:03,000
Just act the part of a good Magical Beast
and there won't be a problem.

113
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:22,000
She keeps saying her name's not Reina.

114
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:24,000
Okay, what is it, then?

115
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:28,000
For the last time, my name is not Reina!
All right?

116
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:31,000
So stop it. Don't call me that.

117
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:33,000
My name is Kite!

118
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:36,000
[intense music playing]

119
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:43,000
Gon! [grunts] Killua!

120
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:13,000
Normally, I would recommend
that he be transported to a specialist.

121
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:17,000
But until he can be taken off
life support, it's too risky.

122
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:31,000
I see. Then we'll just have to bring
the specialist to us.

123
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:35,000
Considering his heroism,
he deserves at least that much.

124
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:38,000
I'll cover all of the expenses.

125
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:42,000
If necessary,
we'll rebuild the whole hospital.

126
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:48,000
But know this,
we are never going to let Gon die.

127
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:39,000
I wish you'd said,
"Let's get him together."

128
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:47,000
Let's go.

129
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:51,000
[Killua] When you said that, were you
ordering me as your teammate?

130
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:54,000
Or were you telling me as your friend?

131
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:03,000
I know. I'm just sulking.

132
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:32,000
But this time,
I won't let you off the hook.

133
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:37,000
You'd better apologize!

134
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:40,000
I'm going to make you better.

135
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:43,000
You hear me?

136
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:48,000
I swear!
I'm gonna make you apologize!

137
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:01,000
So, I'm assembling specialists.

138
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:05,000
I'll use Hide and Seek to transport
the equipment and the medical staff.

139
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:25,000
I'm going to save Gon.

140
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:27,000
[gasps]

141
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:30,000
Go ahead and get the doctors,

142
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:32,000
because he's gonna need 'em…

143
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:36,000
right up until I get back.

144
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:49,000
[Knov] Killua?

145
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:05,000
[static crackling]

146
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:06,000
[tape rattles]

147
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:11,000
Uh, my name is Netero.

148
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:14,000
I'm resigning as chairman,
so please take care.

149
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:27,000
If you don't reach a 95% quorum,
then call for a revote.

150
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:35,000
I'd say it's a level-D difficulty.

151
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:12,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

152
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:31,000
[upbeat music playing]

153
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:33,000
[Gon] Next time, "Debate Among Zodiacs."

154
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:36,000
I won't say anything
until I've seen your face.

155
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:38,000
[Killua] I'm going to make you better.

156
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:41,000
I swear! I'll make you apologize!

157
00:23:43,000 --> 00:23:46,000
[singer singing in Japanese]
